senses.gloss:
प्र-माथ, अस्, m. stirring about, agitation; tor-
menting, torturing, afflicting, paining; killing;
tearing; forcible abduction, rape [cf. द्रौपदी-प्˚];
violence; N. of one of the sons of Dhṛta-rāṣṭra;
of one of the attendants of Skanda; of a Dānava;
(आस्), m. pl. epithet of the fiends attendant upon
Śiva (= प्र-मथ).

प्रमि प्र-मि (see rt. 1. मि), cl. 5. P. A.
-मिनोति, -मिनुते, -मातुम्, to erect, build (Ved.);
to judge, observe, perceive.

प्र-मृत, अस्, आ, अम्, dead, deceased; with-
drawn or gone out of sight; covered, concealed;
(अम्), n. death; tillage, cultivation.

प्रमृज् प्र-मृज्, cl. 2. P. -मार्ष्टि, -मार्जि-
तुम्, -मार्ष्टुम्, to wash out, wash, clean, cleanse;
to wash off, wipe off, wipe away; to wipe out, re-
move, expel, rid one's self of; to rub gently, stroke,
pass the hand over, rub; to make ready, prepare;
to render unavailing, frustrate.
